<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aloysius Gonzaga</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1568–1591</span> · Also known as Saint Aloysius, Luigi Gonzaga</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aloysius Gonzaga was an Italian noble and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuit</a> saint. The eldest son of the Marquis of Castiglione, he gave up his rights of succession to his brother to join the Society of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesus">Jesus</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in 1585. He died aged 23 after nursing victims of an epidemic in Rome. Canonised in 1726, he became the patron saint of young people.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aloysius-gonzaga.jpg" alt="Aloysius Gonzaga" width="320" height="423" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Guercino · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Vocation_of_Saint_Aloysius_Gonzaga.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
